### Description of the problem / feature request:

Since bazel 5.0.0, Querying reverse dependencies of a cc_proto_library returns wrong results, including lots of interal dependencies rather than reverse dependencies.

### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.

Using a minimal example available [here](https://github.com/skeptic-monkey/bazel_bug_rdeps), run the following commands:

```
➜  ~/Downloads/bazel-5.0.0-linux-x86_64 cquery "rdeps(//..., //src:myproto)"
INFO: Analyzed 4 targets (0 packages loaded, 0 targets configured).
INFO: Found 4 targets...
//src:myproto (28ff575)
//src:myproto_cc (28ff575)
@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:toolchain_type (28ff575)
@local_config_platform//:host (28ff575)
@com_google_protobuf//:cc_toolchain (28ff575)
@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:toolchain (28ff575)
@com_google_protobuf//:protoc (5601329)
//src:myproto.proto (null)
@local_config_cc//:cc-compiler-k8 (28ff575)
//src_native:myproto (28ff575)
//src_native:myproto.proto (null)
@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:compiler (28ff575)
@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:current_cc_toolchain (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:protobuf (28ff575)
@zlib//:zlib (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:protobuf_lite (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:wrappers_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:any_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:duration_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:compiler_plugin_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:api_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:empty_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:field_mask_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:source_context_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:struct_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:descriptor_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:timestamp_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:type_proto (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:cc_toolchain (28ff575)
//src_native:myproto_cc (28ff575)
@com_github_protocolbuffers_protobuf//:msvc (28ff575)
INFO: Elapsed time: 0.155s
INFO: 0 processes.
INFO: Build completed successfully, 0 total actions

```
When using bazel 4.2.2, the result is **correct**:

```
➜  ~/Downloads/bazel-4.2.2-linux-x86_64 cquery "rdeps(//..., //src:myproto)"
Starting local Bazel server and connecting to it...
INFO: Analyzed 4 targets (22 packages loaded, 467 targets configured).
INFO: Found 4 targets...
//src:myproto (96d6638)
//src:myproto_cc (96d6638)
INFO: Elapsed time: 5.401s
INFO: 0 processes.
INFO: Build completed successfully, 0 total actions
```

### What operating system are you running Bazel on?

Ubuntu 20.04.1 LTS

### What's the output of `bazel info release`?

release 5.0.0

###  Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?

Found nothing so far.

### Any other information, logs, or outputs that you want to share?

I tried to use both native rules (cc_library, cc_proto_library) and the rules coming from `bazelbuild/rules_cc` and `bazelbuild/rules_proto/`

I also tried a pre release of the version 6.0.0, and the bug is still there.

But using bazel query instead of cquery works:
```
➜  ~/Downloads/bazel-5.0.0-linux-x86_64 query --universe_scope=//... "allrdeps(//src:myproto)"
//src:myproto
//src:myproto_cc
Loading: 0 packages loaded
```

When there are security updates for a piece of our software, any software depending on that will also need updating. E.g. flattentool -> Cove, Cove -> Resource Projects ETL

It's probably useful to log these reverse dependencies somehow (currently the list if small and lives in my head).

